{
	title: 'System prompt: who, where, and what changed',
	description: 'Every provider request carries a system prompt built by the host at request time: a short identity, the date, the session cwd, the model, and the contents of AGENTS.md files found from the cwd upwards (nothing else: there is no home AGENTS.md). Changes the model must know about reach it as <meta> notes in front of the next prompt, like turn ends do (tasks/nn): /cd (new cwd), model switch. Keep the system prompt identical between requests of a session unless its inputs changed, so prompt caching keeps working; test that. Reference: the old SYSTEM.md in the Hal home.',
	status: 'done',
	needs: ['et'],
	notes: [
		"src/host/system-prompt.ts: systemPrompt.build({ cwd, model, now }) is pure over its inputs (and the AGENTS.md files it reads): identity, <date> (local YYYY-MM-DD, weekday: changes at midnight, not per request), <cwd>, <model>, then each AGENTS.md as <file path=...>, outermost first. host.runTurn builds it per provider round from sessions.open(id).cwd and the turn's model; synthetic models get none. anthropic.ts puts it after the OAuth identity block with cache_control.",
		'Only AGENTS.md files on the path from the filesystem root to the cwd are read. There is no "home AGENTS.md": an earlier task text invented it, and the user rejected it.',
		"Changes: host.change(id, { cwd?, model? }) saves session meta, broadcasts meta and appends a `change` history record only for values that really changed. Context gained `model` and `setModel` beside setCwd, for /model (task 0x). replay.toMessages collects change records (latest value per key) into <meta> lines after the [HH:MM] and end note of the next prompt; replay.withoutCommands drops them (not a turn: states and recover ignore them), replay.current keeps them across an edit, transcript shows nothing for them (the command's output already says it)."
	]
}
